{ "type": "Feature", "properties": { "ZoneNumber": "12", "ZoneColor": "Yellow", "ZoneCat": "Definitely Declining", "ZoneNumeri": 12, "ZoneDesc": "The Union hill section (P-23) is principally inhabited by Jewish people of the poorer class. South of Oak Hill (R-22) between Dartmouth and Grafton Streets is the French section. Much of this section, especially toward the east in the neighborhood of Bedford Avenue and Revere Street (S-24) is low lying land even swampy in some places. The area is mostly composed of the poorer class. There are many old three-deckers built from 30 to 50 years ago, a number of which have no central heating system, and lack other modern conveniences. Small single houses are scattered through the area, many in need of repair.", "GlobalID": "d8950b07-c3e2-4bf2-b63a-db87be133f03", "OBJECTID": 4, "Shape__Area": 89429315.229614258, "Shape__Length": 55038.15728401269 }, "geometry": { "type": "Polygon", "coordinates": [ [ [ -71.796991936168197, 42.253686542732801 ], [ -71.798210332159101, 42.254054895800799 ], [ -71.793775935989601, 42.2586593000024 ], [ -71.790396184220299, 42.256719881768397 ], [ -71.785074474463798, 42.255764041156198 ], [ -71.762116328483501, 42.262448262902701 ], [ -71.759215102740399, 42.2628682642897 ], [ -71.758698431698804, 42.2552990383668 ], [ -71.7558227971235, 42.253117394345097 ], [ -71.762005124399806, 42.248453149651603 ], [ -71.758181761621103, 42.244526452298501 ], [ -71.749450024700394, 42.2496673260856 ], [ -71.748132514634506, 42.247936478728299 ], [ -71.748881687342703, 42.247884811870399 ], [ -71.749114188575902, 42.247083971384797 ], [ -71.748804186931295, 42.246618969004501 ], [ -71.748571684437096, 42.2455856272868 ], [ -71.747796678400306, 42.245353124865403 ], [ -71.747331675126603, 42.244965621493698 ], [ -71.747073340011895, 42.244242282388399 ], [ -71.746079706036397, 42.243847431395999 ], [ -71.742327383642703, 42.2429664251517 ], [ -71.737624028300601, 42.241889537953497 ], [ -71.745639029927304, 42.2